.TH NINY 1 "October 2026" "SDE" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
niny \- Niny text editor for the Selviana Desktop Environment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B niny
[\fIOPTION\fR...] [\fB+\fILINE\fR] [\fIFILE\fR[\fB:\fILINE\fR[\fB:\fICOLUMN\fR]]|\fIURI\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B niny
is the text editor of SDE, written for SDE with SDE-FLTK and cairo by the
DebION Dev-Team. It opens each file in a tab, highlights the syntax of C,
C++, Python, shell, JavaScript, TypeScript, JSON, HTML, XML, CSS, Markdown,
INI/configuration files, Rust, Go, Makefiles, YAML and diffs, and stays
responsive with files of tens of megabytes.
.PP
Files given on the command line open in the running Niny window of the
display; a file that does not exist yet is created when it is first saved.
Local
.B file://
URIs are accepted.
.PP
Character encodings (UTF-8, UTF-8 with BOM, UTF-16, ISO-8859-1 and
Windows-1252) and line endings (LF, CRLF, CR) are detected when a file is
opened and kept when it is saved; both can be changed in the status bar.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI + LINE
Put the cursor on \fILINE\fR of the next file.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new\-window
Open a separate window instead of handing the files to the running one.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the options.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Ctrl+Shift+P
Command palette (every command); \fBCtrl+P\fR quickly opens files and
\fBCtrl+G\fR goes to a line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+F, Ctrl+H, F3, Shift+F3
Find, find and replace (with case, whole word and regular expression
options), next and previous match.
.TP
.B Ctrl+N, Ctrl+O, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Shift+S, Ctrl+W, Ctrl+Shift+T
New, open, save, save as, close and reopen the last closed document.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Shift+Z, Ctrl+Y
Undo and redo.
.TP
.B Ctrl+D, Ctrl+Shift+K, Alt+Up, Alt+Down, Ctrl+/
Duplicate, delete or move lines; toggle comments.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Plus, Ctrl+Minus, Ctrl+0, Alt+Z, F9
Zoom, word wrap and the side panel.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/sde/niny.conf
Settings (also changed in Niny's Settings window).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/niny/
Session, recent files and backups of unsaved changes, used to restore
documents after a crash or when quitting with unsaved changes.
